f Stroganoff","dish/beef-stroganoff"],["Bell's (restaurant)","dish/bell-s-restaurant"],["Belmond Le Manoir aux Quat'Saisons","dish/belmond-le-manoir-aux-quat-saisons"],["Beluga (restaurant)","dish/beluga-restaurant"],["Berowra Waters Inn","dish/berowra-waters-inn"],["Beurre maître d'hôtel","dish/beurre-maitre-d-hotel"],["Beurre manié","dish/beurre-manie"],["Bisque (food)","dish/bisque-food"],["Bistro 990","dish/bistro-990"],["Bistro Agnes","dish/bistro-agnes"],["Bistro Jeanty","dish/bistro-jeanty"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/98/Mandarin_Oriental_Hong_Kong_Pierre_Restaurant.jpg/500px-Mandarin_Oriental_Hong_Kong_Pierre_Restaurant.jpg","w":500,"h":294,"by":"Mandarin Oriental Hotel Group","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mandarin_Oriental_Hong_Kong_Pierre_Restaurant.jpg"}},"ingredient/thousand-island-dressing":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/thousand-island-dressing","n":"Thousand Island dressing","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Thousand Island dressing is a creamy salad dressing and condiment made from a base of mayonnaise and usually ketchup or tomato purée and chopped pickles, and typically including a variety of other ingredients. It was initially popularized in the Thousand Islands region of the upper Saint Lawrence River spanning New York and Canada.  Historically a salad dressing, it has been widely adopted by fast food chains as a \"special\" or \"secret\" sauce of their own variation based on the Thousand Island recipe."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-thousand-island-dressing"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thousand_Island_dressing"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Reuben sandwich","dish/reuben-sandwich"]]],["Jewish cuisine","cuisine/jewish-cuisine",[["Reuben sandwich","dish/reuben-sandwich"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Corned beef","ingredient/corned-beef"],["Russian dressing","ingredient/russian-dressing"],["Rye bread","ingredient/rye-bread"],["Sauerkraut","ingredient/sauerkraut"],["Swiss cheese (North America)","ingredient/swiss-cheese-north-america"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/f/fa/Thousand-Island-Dressing.jpg/500px-Thousand-Island-Dressing.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Rainer Z ...","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thousand-Island-Dressing.jpg"}},"ingredient/corn-tortilla":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/corn-tortilla","n":"Corn tortilla","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 2 cuisines","intro":[["In Mexico and Central America, a corn tortilla or just tortilla is a type of thin, unleavened flatbread, made from hominy, that is the whole kernels of maize treated with alkali to improve their nutrition in a process called nixtamalization. A simple dough made of ground hominy, salt and water is then formed into flat discs and cooked on a very hot surface, generally an iron griddle called a comal. A similar flatbread from South America, called an arepa (made with ground maize, not hominy, and typically much thicker than tortillas), also predates the arrival of Europeans to America."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-corn-tortilla"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corn_tortilla"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine",[["Taco","dish/taco"],["Tortilla soup","dish/tortilla-soup"]]],["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Taco","dish/taco"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Flour tortilla","ingredient/flour-tortilla"],["Protein_(nutrient)","ingredient/protein-nutrient"],["Tortilla","ingredient/tortilla"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/ef/Mexican_tortilla.jpg/500px-Mexican_tortilla.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"David Boté Estrada","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mexican_tortilla.jpg"}},"dish/teremok":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/teremok","n":"Teremok","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Russian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Teremok is a Russian fast food chain that primarily specialises in traditional Russian dishes such as blini, pelmeni, and kvass and borscht.  Founded in 1998 by Mikhail Goncharov, their menu was adapted from the recipes of Goncharov's mother."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-teremok"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teremok"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Russian cuisine","cuisine/russian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Olga's Flavor Factory","ref":"site/olgasflavorfactory-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"olgasflavorfactory.com","note":"Russian-born home cook Olga's blog, with a dedicated Russian recipes category.","url":"https://www.olgasflavorfactory.com/category/russianrecipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Russian cuisine","links":[["Aspic","dish/aspic"],["Baba (cake)","dish/baba-cake"],["Beef Stroganoff","dish/beef-stroganoff"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Borscht","dish/borscht"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Cabbage soup","dish/cabbage-soup"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["Chicken Kiev","dish/chicken-kiev"],["Chrain","dish/chrain"],["Dressed herring","dish/dressed-herring"],["Forshmak","dish/forshmak"],["Goulash","dish/goulash"],["Gugelhupf","dish/gugelhupf"],["Kachka (restaurant)","dish/kachka-restaurant"],["Karelian pasty","dish/karelian-pasty"],["Kasha","dish/kasha"],["Khrenovina sauce","dish/khrenovina-sauce"],["Kolach (bread)","dish/kolach-bread"],["Kringle","dish/kringle"],["Medovukha","dish/medovukha"],["Mimosa salad","dish/mimosa-salad"],["Mors (drink)","dish/mors-drink"],["Nesselrode pudding","dish/nesselrode-pudding"],["Okroshka","dish/okroshka"],["Olivier salad","dish/olivier-salad"],["Pancake","dish/pancake"],["Paska (bread)","dish/paska-bread"],["Pâté","dish/pate"],["Pelmeni","dish/pelmeni"],["Pie","dish/pie"],["Pirozhki","dish/pirozhki"],["Polonaise sauce","dish/polonaise-sauce"],["Potato pancake","dish/potato-pancake"],["Pozharsky cutlet","dish/pozharsky-cutlet"],["Rassolnik","dish/rassolnik"],["Sauerkraut","dish/sauerkraut"],["Shchi","dish/shchi"],["Solyanka","dish/solyanka"],["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/7/71/Teremok_%28Moscow%2C_Bratislavskaya_metro_station%2C_October_2023%29.jpg/500px-Teremok_%28Moscow%2C_Bratislavskaya_metro_station%2C_October_2023%29.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Brateevsky","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Teremok_(Moscow%2C_Bratislavskaya_metro_station%2C_October_2023).jpg"}},"ingredient/rogan-josh":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/rogan-josh","n":"Rogan josh","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Rogan josh; English: /ˌroʊɡən ˈdʒɒʃ/), also spelled roghan josh or roghan ghosht, is an aromatic curried meat dish originating in the Kashmir Valley of Jammu and Kashmir, India. It is one of the main dishes in the wazwan, the traditional multi-course Kashmiri feast. Rogan josh is made with red meat—traditionally mutton or goat, coloured and flavoured primarily by alkanet flower (or root) and Kashmiri red chillies. In the West, tomatoes are often used instead."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-rogan-josh"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rogan_josh"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Kashmiri cuisine","cuisine/kashmiri-cuisi